[{:adr/consequences "{:only_otete_orderable \"only Otete is actually orderable at this ADR's acceptance; a\\n                         per-character Hitogata biped remains aspirational until giemon's own\\n                         design track ships a real fixture/BOM\", :scale_is_followup \"the procurement pipeline's durability at scale (a real contracted EMS\\n                      relationship, live supplier onboarding, real shipment tracking) is a\\n                      business/operations follow-up, not built by this ADR\", :new_cross_repo_deps \"net-babiniku now depends on kotoba-lang/giemon and kotoba-lang/robotics\\n                        for anything touching a physical body -- real cross-repo dependencies,\\n                        not aspirational references\", :open_followup \"registering a net-babiniku-specific procurement actor (vs. reusing/forking\\n                 yoro-supply's cells directly) is an implementation decision left open\"}", :adr/authoritative_for ["a net-babiniku persona may declare an associated physical Giemon body -- this ADR wires\n    existing Giemon products to character identities, it does not design a new robot" "only Giemon Otete (6-DOF arm + crawler, shipping, real BOM) is orderable under this ADR --\n    Hitogata (17-axis biped) remains :in-design with no articulation fixture and is NOT\n    presented as purchasable, per the honest-default principle" "any path from a persona's proposed behavior to a physical Giemon body's joint commands\n    must pass through kotoba-lang/robotics' safety gate exactly as kotoba.giemon.governor\n    already requires for Giemon Kaigo -- no LLM-to-actuator shortcut" "ordering/procurement reuses the yoro-supply Pregel-cell actor shape and cloud-itonami's\n    plm.cljc BOM primitives rather than building a new EC/ordering stack" "the robot purchase-order payment rail is a distinct, ordinary fiat rail from\n    ADR-2607062200's adult-content-gated chat-monetization rail -- must not be conflated"], :adr/supersedes [], :adr/superseded_by [], :adr/topic "net-babiniku-giemon-embodiment", :adr/related ["90-docs/adr/2607062200-net-babiniku-onlyfans-style-creator-monetization.md" "90-docs/adr/2607011000-cloud-itonami-robotics-premise-and-isic-21-21.md" "90-docs/adr/2607020000-kotoba-lang-giemon-product-line.md" "orgs/gftdcojp/ai-gftd-apps-gftdcojp/90-docs/adr/2604252100-robotics-product-manufacturing-package.md.edn"], :adr/status "proposed", :adr/id "adr-2607062210-net-babiniku-giemon-humanoid-embodiment-procurement", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/last_verified "2026-07-06", :adr/decision "{:embodiment_scope {:what \"physical embodiment is optional and per-character, not a new robot design -- a\\n          net-babiniku persona may declare an associated Giemon body; this ADR wires existing\\n          (or eventually-existing) Giemon products to character identities\"}, :mvp_orderable_body {:what \"Giemon Otete (6-DOF arm + crawler) only, NOT Hitogata\", :why \"Hitogata is :in-design with no articulation fixture -- no real BOM exists to order.\\n         Per the honest-default principle from ADR-2607062200 (no vaporware presented as\\n         purchasable), Hitogata is not orderable under this ADR. Otete is real, shipping, and\\n         has a canonical BOM (fixtures/giemon_arm6/) -- that is what 発注できるように can\\n         actually mean today.\", :future \"when Hitogata's own design work (tracked independently under\\n            giemon/ADR-2605142200) reaches a real fixture and BOM, it becomes eligible for\\n            the same ordering path with no changes to this ADR's decisions -- this ADR does\\n            not pull that design work forward\"}, :no_actuation_shortcut {:what \"the persona/governor from ADR-2607062200 proposes character behavior only\\n          (dialogue/emotion/motion-cue) for the VIRTUAL VRM body. Any path from a character's\\n          behavior to a PHYSICAL Giemon body's joint commands must pass through\\n          kotoba.robotics' gate exactly as kotoba.giemon.governor already requires for Kaigo\\n          -- no exception to :high/:safety-critical human sign-off, :actuate/:move/:grasp/\\n          :emit are never dispatched directly from a persona proposal\"}, :ordering_pipeline {:reuse \"yoro-supply's Pregel-cell shape (supplier_selection -> order_placement ->\\n           manufacture_track -> shipment -> delivery_verify) and cloud-itonami's plm.cljc\\n           primitives, rather than a new ordering stack\", :mechanism \"a per-character Otete BOM (arm/bom giemon-arm6 <realization-variant>) becomes\\n              the projectBOM input to that flow, packaged per ADR-2604252100's\\n              manufacturing-package manifest (BOM CSV via kotoba.giemon.export, plus\\n              STEP/3MF/Gerber/inspection-plan as applicable) as the artifact an EMS actually\\n              RFQs against\"}, :payment_rail {:what \"ordinary physical-goods fiat transaction, no adult-content PSP constraint -- can\\n          use the org's existing Stripe-shaped billing schema (kotoba-lang/com-stripe,\\n          net-kotobase/billing.cljc pattern) for the purchase-order payment leg\", :must_stay_distinct_from \"ADR-2607062200's adult-content-gated chat-monetization rail --\\n                            one is adult-content-gated recurring billing, the other is a\\n                            one-time hardware PO; must not be conflated\"}, :character_body_binding {:what \"which Giemon SKU (today: only Otete) a persona 'owns' as its physical embodiment is\\n          a persona-record data field -- cosmetic/identity binding, not a new hardware variant\\n          per character\"}}", :db/id -1, :adr/problem "{:source \"user direction 2026-07-06: design a humanoid robot per net-babiniku character based\\n           on kotoba-lang/giemon, and make it orderable (発注できるように)\", :prior_art {:giemon {:what \"kotoba-lang/giemon (ADR-2605142200): open-hardware robot product line in pure\\n           Clojure -- product metadata, forward kinematics/torque validation, actuator BOM\\n           generator, viewer scene-IR, CSV/JSON export\", :products {:otete \":product/status :shipping, 6-DOF arm + crawler, real articulation fixture\\n             (fixtures/giemon_arm6/, EDN source of truth + URDF parity oracle)\", :hitogata \":in-design, 17-axis biped, NO articulation fixture yet\", :caterpillar \":in-design, dual-track UGV\", :giemon_kaigo \"ADR-2605142300, in-home elder-care application consuming these products --\\n                    a distinct use case from what's asked here\"}, :governance_delegation \"giemon does NOT own safety governance -- delegates to\\n                            kotoba-lang/robotics (ADR-2607011000); kotoba.giemon.governor is a\\n                            thin wrapper over it, per giemon's own README\"}, :kotoba_robotics {:what \"orgs/kotoba-lang/robotics/src/kotoba/robotics.cljc -- the one safety contract\\n           every cloud-itonami actuation path (26 industry blueprints) depends on\", :doctrine \"'policy, not control. It does not drive motors; it gives a governor the\\n               records it needs to refuse unsafe actuation before it ever reaches hardware.'\", :safety_classes \"#{:none :low :medium :high :safety-critical}\", :human_sign_off_classes \"#{:high :safety-critical} -- require interrupt-before human\\n                             sign-off\", :action_kinds \"#{:sense :move :grasp :actuate :emit} -- only :sense is read-only\"}, :manufacturing_package_adr {:what \"ai-gftd-apps-gftdcojp/90-docs/adr/2604252100 (Accepted): real-machine control\\n           adapter boundary + manufacturing package definition for physical robot products\", :control_boundary \"AI agent は actuator に直接 command を送ってはならない -- mission\\n                       plan/replan/approval/simulation only; real dispatch goes through a\\n                       safety gateway then an asset-specific adapter (ROS2/MAVLink/VDA5050)\", :manufacturing_package \"CAD/ECAD/CAM/BOM/routing/inspection/firmware/calibration bundled\\n                            together -- no single-file standard exists for real hardware\"}, :procurement_actors {:yoro_supply \"app-aozora/20-actors/yoro-supply (ADR-2605250850): building-materials\\n                  procurement actor, 5 Pregel cells (supplier_selection/order_placement/\\n                  manufacture_track/shipment/delivery_verify), lexicon-typed PO/RFQ events,\\n                  14 Constitutional Gates, input = projectBOM\", :cloud_itonami \"itonami/store.cljc (procurement line-items, UNSPSC/supplier/qty/cost),\\n                    itonami/governor.cljc (HARD-holds unregistered-supplier lineage breaks),\\n                    cloud_itonami/plm.cljc (item/bom-edge/change-order/make-buy/unit-cost/\\n                    mbom-rows via kotoba.plm.item)\", :conclusion \"no general-purpose EC/ordering stack exists or should be built -- the\\n                actor-based procurement shape is the established pattern for 'turn a BOM into\\n                a real purchase order'\"}}}", :adr/alternatives "[{:option \"design an all-new bespoke humanoid robot for net-babiniku instead of reusing\\n            giemon\", :rejected_because \"giemon is the existing open-hardware product line with real\\n                      BOM/kinematics/governor/manufacturing-package precedent; a bespoke\\n                      design duplicates real engineering work for no benefit, the same\\n                      reasoning ADR-2607051800 already used to reject reimplementing VRM\\n                      rendering glue\"} {:option \"let the persona governor command giemon joints directly, skipping kotoba.robotics'\\n            gate\", :rejected_because \"violates the repo's non-negotiable 'AI agent never commands actuators\\n                      directly' doctrine (kotoba.robotics docstring, itonami.governor's\\n                      no-actuation invariant, ADR-2604252100's safety-gateway requirement)\"} {:option \"build a bespoke EC/ordering system for robot purchases\", :rejected_because \"yoro-supply's Pregel-cell procurement actor and cloud-itonami/plm.cljc\\n                      already implement this shape; reuse over reinvention\"} {:option \"default to Hitogata (biped) as the flagship orderable body since it reads as more\\n            'humanoid'/VTuber-appropriate\", :rejected_because \"Hitogata is still :in-design per giemon's own README, with no real BOM;\\n                      presenting it as orderable would violate the honest-default principle\\n                      applied in ADR-2607062200\"}]", :adr/authoritative true, :adr/title "ADR-2607062210: net-babiniku characters -- optional physical embodiment via\n          kotoba-lang/giemon, procurable through an EMS ordering pipeline"}]